on":87,"layoutDesc":155,"handNote":159,"date":240,"places":245,"geo":253,"country":77,"provenance":247,"provenanceGeo":257,"region":81,"settlement":247,"repository":260,"idno":264,"textLang":267,"tmNumber":130,"facsimile":269,"letterHeights":276,"publications":314,"zotero":317,"keywords":320,"html":328,"bibl":329,"bulletinDateSort":122,"citedRangeSort":332,"languageSort":89,"materialSort":139,"typeSort":34},"ISic003337","Funerary inscription for Eirena",{"_":127},"edited",[129,131,132,133,134],{"_":130,"type":16},"645584",{"type":18},{"type":20},{"type":22},{"type":25},null,{"_":34,"ana":35,"ref":36},{"_":38,"ana":39,"ref":40},{"_":139,"ana":140,"type":44,"subtype":141,"resp":143,"ref":47,"placeName":144,"note":151},"Very fine-grained, veined, white marble, likely Pavonazzetto. Digital microscopy: indistinguishable fabric. Scribbly veins, maybe a limestone (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)\n","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Pavonazzetto",[142],"Pavonazzetto","#Coccato",{"type":145,"ref":146,"location":149},"provenance",{"_":147,"target":148},"Bakakale","https://www.geonames.org/12207392/iscehisar-bucagi.html",{"geo":150},"38.86194,30.75028",{"_":152,"ref":153}," Petrographic imagery at ",{"_":154,"target":154},"https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic003337",{"layout":156},{"p":157,"rs":158,"damage":87},"Ten lines of Greek filling the available space, decreasing notably in size in the second five lines",{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},{"lettering":160,"dimensions":161},"The letters are engraved in a fairly plain, square fashion, with simple serifs. Alpha is mostly with broken bar, sometimes with an extended upper serif, although there is a straight bar example in line 7 and in lines 8 and 10 straight bar descending to left foot; beta is closed, with larger lower eye, generally horizontal along the base; delta varies between regular triangle and oblique lower bar with extended serif above; epsilon has straight bars of equal length, except for instances in lines 9 and 10 when it is lunate; theta is ovoid with connecting straight bar; kappa has short tails; lambda sometimes has an extended upper serif; mu varies between a form with vertical first and last hastae and short middle strokes meeting above the line and cursive form comparable to a lower-case mu in line 9; omicron is full size in the first few lines, but increasingly is smaller and mid-line; sigma is consistently lunate, but more often formed of three straight strokes; less often a single curved stroke; omega is consistently lunate, and sometimes smaller and mid-line. The eta and nu are in ligature in lines 5, 6 and 7. In line 5 the omicron in the final word is inscribed above the other letters (due to omission?). The last two/three words of the last line are enclosed between a pair of christograms. Small hedera occur in lines 1, 3, 5, and 10.",[162,166,171,176,181,184,190,195,200,205,211,214,218,221,225,229,231,235,238],{"type":63,"l":64,"from":65,"to":65,"h":163,"unit":66,"atLeast":164,"atMost":165},"12-18","12","18",{"type":63,"l":167,"from":70,"to":70,"h":168,"unit":66,"atLeast":169,"atMost":170},"Line 2","14-19","14","19",{"type":63,"l":172,"from":173,"to":173,"h":174,"unit":66,"atLeast":164,"atMost":175},"Line 3","line3","12-22","22",{"type":63,"l":177,"from":178,"to":178,"h":179,"unit":66,"atLeast":180,"atMost":175},"Line 4","line4","8-22","8",{"type":63,"l":182,"from":183,"to":183,"h":163,"unit":66,"atLeast":164,"atMost":165},"Line 5","line5",{"type":63,"l":185,"from":186,"to":186,"h":187,"unit":66,"atLeast":188,"atMost":189},"Line 6","line6","9-16","9","16",{"type":63,"l":191,"from":192,"to":192,"h":193,"unit":66,"atLeast":194,"atMost":169},"Line 7","line7","7-14","7",{"type":63,"l":196,"from":197,"to":197,"h":198,"unit":66,"atLeast":199,"atMost":164},"Line 8","line8","6-12","6",{"type":63,"l":201,"from":202,"to":202,"h":203,"unit":66,"atLeast":199,"atMost":204},"Line 9","line9","6-10","10",{"type":63,"l":206